## Why This Is Asked

Tests real‑world, low‑level queue design under NUMA and kernel-bypass constraints. Evaluates API clarity, memory ordering discipline, and practical safeguards against ABA and false sharing.

## Key Concepts

- NUMA affinity and cross-socket latency
- Kernel-bypass, zero-copy semantics
- Per-slot sequence counters to prevent ABA
- Cache-line alignment and padding to avoid false sharing
- Memory ordering: CAS on tail/head with acq_rel fences

